Contract: `totalSize(paths []string) (int64, error)` opens each path in turn, adds its size, and returns the sum. Because `paths` can be arbitrarily long (tens of thousands of entries), it must hold at most one file open at a time so it never exhausts the process file-descriptor limit. Does this implementation meet the contract? If not, name the bug and the minimal fix.

```go
func totalSize(paths []string) (int64, error) {
    var total int64
    for _, p := range paths {
        f, err := os.Open(p)
        if err != nil {
            return 0, err
        }
        defer f.Close()
        fi, err := f.Stat()
        if err != nil {
            return 0, err
        }
        total += fi.Size()
    }
    return total, nil
}
```
